 CODE 
Art. 2.3.86. 
Data controller 
The Royal Federation of Belgian Notaries, hereinafter referred to as "the controller", is responsible for the management and organisation of the central register of matrimonial property agreements.
The Manager shall be considered, as far as the central register of matrimonial agreements is concerned, as the controller, within the meaning of Article 4, 7), of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 27 April 2016 on the protection of individuals with regard to the processing of personal data and on the free movement of such data, and repealing Directive 95/46/EC.
 The administrator shall appoint a data protection officer. This person is more specifically responsible for   
1¡ providing qualified advice on the protection of privacy, the security of personal data and information and the processing thereof; 
2¡ informing and advising the data controller processing personal data of its obligations under this law and the general framework for the protection of data and privacy;   
3¡ establishing, implementing, updating and monitoring a security and privacy protection policy; 
4¡ acting as the contact point for the Data Protection Authority; 
5¡ carrying out other tasks relating to privacy protection and security that are determined by the King, after obtaining the opinion of the Data Protection Authority.
 In the performance of his or her duties, the Data Protection Officer acts completely independently and reports directly to the manager.
 The King may, after obtaining the opinion of the Data Protection Authority, determine the rules on the basis of which the Data Protection Officer carries out his duties.
